---
title: "Free Tool to Blur Faces in Photos Online"
description: "Blur, pixelate or black out faces in a photo. Click a face to keep it visible. Face detection runs in your browser. Your photo is never uploaded."
faq:
  - q: "Is the Face Blur tool free?"
    a: "Yes. The tool is free, with no account, no sign-up, no watermark and no limit on how often you use it."
  - q: "Is my photo uploaded to a server?"
    a: "No. The page has no server code. Face detection and blurring run in your browser, and your photo never leaves your device. The only downloads are the small face model and the code that runs it, which contain no user data."
  - q: "Can someone undo the blur?"
    a: "No. The tool does not put a filter on top of the face. It shrinks the face area to a few pixels and stretches it back, or fills it with black, and saves a new image. The original detail is not in the downloaded file, so there is nothing to recover. At a low strength, a blur can still show the rough shape of a face, so use a high strength or the Black box style when it matters."
  - q: "Does it find every face?"
    a: "No automatic tool is perfect. Very small, turned or partly covered faces can be missed, and sometimes an object is marked as a face. Look at the whole photo before you share it. Drag on the photo to add a box, and click a box to turn it off."
  - q: "Can I keep some faces visible?"
    a: "Yes. Click a face box to show that face. Click it again to hide it. This is useful when you want to blur everyone except yourself."
  - q: "Can I blur things that are not faces, such as a license plate or a name badge?"
    a: "Yes. Drag on the photo to draw a box over any area. The tool hides it with the same style as the faces."
  - q: "Which file types does it support?"
    a: "JPG, PNG and WebP photos. The downloaded photo keeps the same format as the original. Very large photos, over 16 megapixels, are made smaller first."
  - q: "Does the downloaded photo keep its location data?"
    a: "No. The downloaded photo is a new file. It does not keep the original's metadata, such as GPS location, camera model and date."
---

